        "original_id": "61c36f0d-2505-5e98-a691-8b704080b203",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brian Olsen, Mike Kyle, Frank Fertitta III, Lorenzo Fertitta\n- Companies: Zuffa, Station Casinos, Semaphore Entertainment Group\n- Organizations: WEC, UFC\n- Events: WEC 20\n- Topics: Heavyweight championship abolition, organizational purchase\n\nFacts:\n- In January 2001, Frank Fertitta III and Lorenzo Fertitta, who were Station Casinos executives, founded Zuffa in Las Vegas, Nevada.\n- In January 2001, Frank Fertitta III and Lorenzo Fertitta founded Zuffa to serve as the parent entity of the UFC after purchasing the UFC from Semaphore Entertainment Group.\n- At WEC 20, the main event was a heavyweight bout between Brian Olsen and Mike Kyle.\n- Brian Olsen was the last WEC Heavyweight Champion before the championship was abolished when Zuffa purchased the organization.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
